  m_text: 'Why does Ya Kun Kopi taste so distinct? In the 1940s, Ah Koon roasted
    coffee beans over firewood at the back of his stall.


    He added margarine
    and sugar during roasting to caramelize the beans. This created the glossy, aromatic,
    and full-bodied ''Nanyang Kopi'' we love today!'
